  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Lyrical, sentimental song in Portuguese that the Rio-born poet-singer Domingos Caldas Barbosa made fashionable in Lisbon in the late eighteenth century, singing to the viola. Through the nineteenth century it became a salon song with piano at the imperial court of Rio de Janeiro and then a street serenade song with violão, and in the early twentieth century singers such as Eduardo das Neves and Mário Pinheiro recorded modinhas for Casa Edison.",
